    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It follows from Corollary <a href="/tag/17C386" data-tag="17C386">5.4.5.16</a> that $\calC _{p/}$ is accessible. It therefore suffices to prove that every diagram $q: K' \rightarrow \calC _{p/}$ has a colimit in $\calC $. We now observe that $(\calC _{p/})_{q/} \simeq \calC _{q'/}$ where $q': K \star K' \rightarrow \calC $ is the map classified by $q$. Since $\calC $ admits small colimits, $\calC _{q'/}$ has an initial object. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
